  "task": "Identify long-lived credentials that grant Amazon Bedrock access and have NOT been used in the last 90 days (i.e., last used before 2026-08-27T10:00:00Z, or never used), and assess which are safe to remove.",
  "context": "User wants an audit of stale long-lived credentials with Bedrock access. Long-lived credentials = IAM user access keys (active and inactive) and Amazon Bedrock long-term API keys (IAM service-specific credentials for bedrock.amazonaws.com, via iam list_service_specific_credentials / get last-used info where available). Current time is 2026-11-25T10:01Z. Start with account 012345678901_1 (IAM is global; use us-east-1), and also cover any other AWS accounts returned by list_associations that this space can access.",
  "criteria": [
    "Determine Bedrock access per IAM user: managed policies (e.g. AmazonBedrockFullAccess, AmazonBedrockReadOnly, AmazonBedrockLimitedAccess-style policies, bedrock-related AWS managed policies), inline policies, group-attached/inline policies, and permission boundaries; include policies with bedrock:* / bedrock-runtime / InvokeModel / Converse actions or wildcard actions (*) that cover Bedrock. Note if access is effectively denied by an explicit Deny or boundary.",
    "For each such credential report: user name, credential type and ID (access key ID — never print secrets), status (Active/Inactive), created date, last-used date, last-used service and region (from get_access_key_last_used; and for Bedrock API keys whatever last-used data is available), how Bedrock access is granted, and days since last use.",
    "Keep only those unused for 90+ days or never used.",
    "For 'safe to remove' judgment: flag as safer to remove if never used or unused 90+ days, and not the user's only credential for something else; flag extra caution if last-used service is something other than Bedrock (key is used for other things — the Bedrock permission may be stale but the key is not idle), if the key is for a service/automation user, if the key was created less than 90 days ago, or if recent CloudTrail activity (use lookup_cloudtrail_events if available, last 90 days) contradicts the IAM last-used data. Note IAM last-used tracking caveats.",
    "Also report counts: total IAM users, total with Bedrock access, total Bedrock-capable credentials, and how many are stale. Also list credentials with Bedrock access that ARE recently used (just IDs and last-used date, briefly) so the user sees the contrast.",
    "Return a concise table-ready summary plus a short list of caveats/permission errors encountered."
  ]
}", "preloaded_skills": ["investigating-infrastructure-changes"]}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit IAM credentials with Bedrock access unused 90+ days"}], "created_at": null}

